WEBVTT

00:03.776 --> 00:05.109
Alan.

00:05.917 --> 00:06.999
Hurry up.

00:07.001 --> 00:08.567
The girls are almost here,
and I'm a...

00:08.569 --> 00:11.837
♪ Hunka hunka rotting love. ♪

00:11.839 --> 00:14.056
ALAN: Sorry, just
finishing up my costume.

00:20.181 --> 00:22.181
Who the hell are
you supposed to be?

00:22.183 --> 00:24.149
You never saw&lt;i> Pretty in Pink?&lt;/i>

00:24.151 --> 00:27.019
Oh, right!
You're Molly Ringwald.

00:27.021 --> 00:28.654
Ha-ha. I-I'm Duckie.

00:28.656 --> 00:31.323
You know, the-the best friend,
the-the scene stealer?

00:31.325 --> 00:34.693
Some would say
the true star of the film.

00:34.695 --> 00:36.529
Who played him, Boy George?
(chuckles)

00:38.165 --> 00:41.083
Hey, what do you think
about zombie Elvis, baby?

00:41.085 --> 00:43.118
And don't be cruel.

00:43.120 --> 00:44.620
It's great.

00:44.622 --> 00:46.622
You look like both
the impersonator at my wedding

00:46.624 --> 00:48.290
and my ex-wife.

00:49.594 --> 00:50.960
Thank you.
Thank you very much.

00:50.962 --> 00:54.630
What decays in Vegas
stays in Vegas.

00:54.632 --> 00:56.632
Oh, hey, uh, did your
friend Stacy say anything

00:56.634 --> 00:58.050
bout the girl she's
bringing for me?

00:58.052 --> 00:59.802
Uh, just that she's supposed
to be really cute,

00:59.804 --> 01:01.670
and she just moved out here
after a tough breakup.

01:01.672 --> 01:03.622
Ooh, hot, lonely
and damaged.

01:03.624 --> 01:05.507
Duckie's getting lucky.

01:06.510 --> 01:08.394
You know, if Duckie
really wants to get lucky,

01:08.396 --> 01:11.063
he'll tell the girls that he's
someone that people remember.

01:11.065 --> 01:12.698
Like Ferris Bueller.

01:14.569 --> 01:17.152
Fine, you win again, Broderick.

01:17.154 --> 01:19.188
God, you know what
I love about Halloween?

01:19.190 --> 01:21.440
You can put “slutty”
in front of any job position,

01:21.442 --> 01:23.409
and it becomes a costume.

01:23.411 --> 01:26.362
Slutty nurse, slutty librarian,
slutty lunch lady.

01:26.364 --> 01:27.997
(groans)

01:27.999 --> 01:29.949
Hey, you didn't know
Mrs. Goobadeck

01:29.951 --> 01:32.701
from Mark Twain Elementary.

01:32.703 --> 01:34.954
She rocked that hairnet.

01:34.956 --> 01:36.538
(groaning):
My chest.

01:36.540 --> 01:38.040
Seriously?
W-What's going on?

01:38.042 --> 01:40.009
I don't know, I can't breathe,
my chest is tight.

01:40.011 --> 01:41.011
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

01:41.012 --> 01:42.127
Here, here. Sit down.

01:42.129 --> 01:44.597
Um... Oh. Uh, well,
uh, don't worry.

01:44.599 --> 01:46.799
I-I'm sure this is
nothing, but, uh...

01:46.801 --> 01:50.552
I'm going to call an ambulance,
just in case.

01:50.554 --> 01:51.887
Just, uh, just stay calm.

01:51.889 --> 01:53.105
You're gonna be fine.

01:53.107 --> 01:55.891
(whispering):
Help! My friend is dying!

01:55.893 --> 01:58.193
I can't settle down, I think
he's having a heart attack.

01:58.195 --> 01:59.895
Oh, my God, I'm having
a heart attack.

01:59.897 --> 02:01.313
Oh. No, no.

02:01.315 --> 02:03.232
I-I'm just saying that
to get them to hurry.

02:03.234 --> 02:04.366
I'm not just saying that.

02:04.368 --> 02:05.534
I think he's headed
toward the light.

02:05.536 --> 02:06.368
(door bell rings)

02:06.370 --> 02:07.903
I can't feel my left arm.

02:07.905 --> 02:09.371
Um, uh, you're gonna be okay.

02:09.373 --> 02:11.573
It's probably just gas.
Try to fart!

02:13.244 --> 02:14.209
Trick...

02:14.211 --> 02:15.661
Or treat.

02:15.663 --> 02:18.080
Oh, ladies. I'm sorry, you just
got here during a bit of a...

02:18.082 --> 02:19.415
Ooh, I can see
your nipples, officer.

02:19.417 --> 02:23.669
Anything you see will
be held against you.

02:24.588 --> 02:26.305
And I'm Harry Potter.

02:26.307 --> 02:28.257
But I'm not so hairy.

02:28.259 --> 02:29.558
She's mine.

02:30.544 --> 02:31.760
(groans)

02:31.762 --> 02:33.178
(farts)

02:34.765 --> 02:37.349
Didn't work!

02:37.373 --> 02:41.373
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 12x01 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">The Ol' Mexican Spinach&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on October 30, 2014

02:41.397 --> 02:47.897
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>

02:50.440 --> 02:52.490
(siren wailing)

02:52.492 --> 02:54.203
Don't worry, we're
almost to the hospital.

02:54.204 --> 02:55.787
Sir, are you taking
any medications?

02:55.789 --> 02:58.457
Well, I take a generic Lipitor
and a women's multi-vitamin.

02:59.676 --> 03:01.343
I mean, just so you know,
I take the women's

03:01.345 --> 03:02.544
'cause it has more iron.

03:03.630 --> 03:05.097
Same price, more iron.

03:05.099 --> 03:06.298
Yes, please.

03:07.668 --> 03:08.767
Is he gonna be okay?

03:08.769 --> 03:10.018
We're doing
all we can, sir.

03:10.020 --> 03:11.720
I can't believe this is
happening, you know?

03:11.722 --> 03:12.854
He's so young!

03:12.856 --> 03:14.606
He leads such
a healthy lifestyle...

03:14.608 --> 03:16.057
Well, except for all the pot.

03:18.061 --> 03:19.277
You know, the-the weed.

03:19.279 --> 03:20.645
The... the ganja.

03:21.565 --> 03:24.199
The ol' Mexican spinach.

03:24.201 --> 03:28.069
Alan, if I live,
I'm going to kill you.

03:28.071 --> 03:30.238
Stop it. You are gonna live.

03:30.240 --> 03:31.573
(chuckles)

03:31.575 --> 03:32.741
Is he gonna live?

03:32.743 --> 03:34.993
We're en route
with a 35-year-old male.

03:34.995 --> 03:37.913
BP is 160/94, pulse is 108.

03:37.915 --> 03:40.365
And he's dressed
as zombie Elvis, over!

03:41.385 --> 03:43.752
I-I don't know if you guys
need to know that.

03:43.754 --> 03:44.769
They don't.

03:47.090 --> 03:48.707
By the way, uh,
I'm dressed as...

03:48.709 --> 03:49.875
Ferris Bueller?

03:49.877 --> 03:51.760
(laughs)

03:51.762 --> 03:54.513
Hey, hey, at least I took
a chance with my costume.

03:54.515 --> 03:56.565
I mean, Elvis and zombies.

03:56.567 --> 03:57.599
It's real original.

03:57.601 --> 03:59.601
Next year, it's vampire Obama.

03:59.603 --> 04:02.187
(Transylvanian accent):
“Yes, we can!”

04:02.189 --> 04:05.440
Excuse me, do you have
anything for the pain?

04:05.442 --> 04:07.993
In my ass?

04:07.995 --> 04:09.361
I know, I know.

04:09.363 --> 04:11.696
I'm just... I'm freaking out
because I'm worried.

04:11.698 --> 04:13.165
I mean, you are my best friend.

04:13.167 --> 04:14.916
And if something were
to happen to you,

04:14.918 --> 04:16.284
I don't know what I would do.

04:16.286 --> 04:17.869
I mean, I-I've already
lost a brother.

04:17.871 --> 04:20.255
I can't lose
you, too!

04:20.257 --> 04:21.873
A-And you're more
of a brother than he was.

04:21.875 --> 04:23.675
And now Jake's in the Army,
and I'm all alone.

04:23.677 --> 04:25.210
And I don't do well
when I'm alone...

04:25.212 --> 04:26.378
Here, breathe.

04:28.515 --> 04:31.016
Thank you.

04:32.269 --> 04:35.687
Am I crazy, or is, uh,
something happening here?

04:39.109 --> 04:41.393
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

04:46.316 --> 04:47.816
Oh, good, uh, you made it.

04:47.818 --> 04:49.734
Uh... Oh, I-I'm sorry I pulled
you out of your Halloween party,

04:49.736 --> 04:50.652
I just figured you'd want to...

04:50.654 --> 04:53.205
I wasn't at a Halloween party.

04:54.291 --> 04:56.074
I-I just assumed,
since you're dressed...

04:56.076 --> 04:57.409
So what happened?

04:57.411 --> 04:59.044
I don't know.

04:59.046 --> 05:00.212
We were about to go out,

05:00.214 --> 05:02.547
and he got chest pains
and suddenly collapsed.

05:02.549 --> 05:04.332
Oh, wow.

05:04.334 --> 05:06.167
He's so young.

05:06.169 --> 05:07.502
So fit.

05:07.504 --> 05:09.521
So not you.

05:10.941 --> 05:14.059
Hope he's okay.

05:14.061 --> 05:17.896
I never thought I'd have a boss
better than your brother,

05:17.898 --> 05:19.931
but Walden is good people.

05:19.933 --> 05:21.733
He's the best.

05:21.735 --> 05:24.936
The guy has the biggest heart
of anyone I have ever met.

05:24.938 --> 05:26.888
Yep, a heart of gold.

05:26.890 --> 05:29.591
Clogged with arterial plaque.

05:29.593 --> 05:31.593
You've been a good
friend to Walden.

05:31.595 --> 05:32.861
He's lucky
to have you.

05:32.863 --> 05:36.865
He's lucky to have you,
too, Sister Berta.

05:36.867 --> 05:38.867
And, listen, um...

05:38.869 --> 05:42.420
if, God forbid,
the worst happens,

05:42.422 --> 05:44.539
I-I just want you
to know that, uh...

05:44.541 --> 05:47.375
you'll always have
a job at the house.

05:47.377 --> 05:50.378
I mean, we'd have to talk
reduced salaries, but, uh...

05:50.380 --> 05:52.764
What makes you think
he'd leave you the house?

05:52.766 --> 05:54.366
I'm his best friend.

05:54.368 --> 05:56.017
There's nobody closer
to him than me.

05:56.019 --> 05:57.435
I clean his underwear.

05:57.437 --> 05:58.970
I&lt;i> wear&lt;/i> his underwear.

05:58.972 --> 06:00.555
(laughs)

06:00.557 --> 06:02.274
Alan Harper?

06:02.276 --> 06:04.059
Oh, oh, that's me.

06:04.061 --> 06:05.727
I'm Dr. Prajneep.

06:05.729 --> 06:07.562
Your friend had a
mild heart attack.

06:07.564 --> 06:09.481
We put in a stent to
clear the blockage.

06:09.483 --> 06:10.332
Is that bad?

06:10.334 --> 06:11.750
In general,

06:11.752 --> 06:13.234
a heart attack is bad.

06:13.236 --> 06:15.453
But, uh, he should
make a full recovery.

06:15.455 --> 06:16.655
Oh, thank God.

06:16.657 --> 06:17.989
Oh, that is
a huge relief.

06:17.991 --> 06:19.908
Um, is there anything
we should do at home?

06:19.910 --> 06:22.577
I just want to make sure
he has all the care he needs.

06:22.579 --> 06:24.913
Uh, any special diet,
exercises, medications?

06:24.915 --> 06:26.214
If it'd help,

06:26.216 --> 06:28.633
I'd chew up his food and
feed him like a baby bird.

06:28.635 --> 06:32.087
How could that
possibly help?

06:32.089 --> 06:34.422
I'll tell you what
doesn't help-- that tone.

06:34.424 --> 06:36.224
Can we see him?

06:36.226 --> 06:37.592
Soon as he's
in recovery.

06:37.594 --> 06:38.843
Any other questions?

06:38.845 --> 06:40.595
Uh, no, we're just happy
that he's gonna be okay.

06:40.597 --> 06:41.597
Thank you.

06:41.598 --> 06:42.814
My pleasure.

06:42.816 --> 06:45.150
By the way,&lt;i> Ferris Bueller&lt;/i>
is my favorite movie.

06:47.571 --> 06:49.654
Wait, B-Berta.
W-Where are you going?

06:49.656 --> 06:51.072
We're not supposed
to go back there yet.

06:51.074 --> 06:52.657
I'm a nun at a hospital.

06:52.659 --> 06:55.327
I can do whatever
the hell I want.

07:01.668 --> 07:04.069
I'm dead.

07:08.208 --> 07:10.241
And I'm in hell.

07:11.194 --> 07:12.861
Relax.

07:12.863 --> 07:14.179
You're in the hospital.

07:14.181 --> 07:16.598
You had a mild heart attack,
but you're gonna be fine.

07:16.600 --> 07:18.316
I don't feel very good.

07:18.318 --> 07:20.552
That's because they put
a stent in your heart.

07:20.554 --> 07:22.971
But also I feel really good.

07:22.973 --> 07:27.192
That's because they put morphine
in your veins.

07:27.194 --> 07:30.011
We should start keeping morphine
in the house.

07:30.013 --> 07:32.697
I know a guy.

07:32.699 --> 07:36.151
Berta, you're so funny.

07:36.153 --> 07:39.320
I would've missed you so much
if I would've died.

07:39.322 --> 07:41.456
Oh, oh, but you don't
have to worry about that.

07:41.458 --> 07:42.540
Y-You're not going anywhere.

07:42.542 --> 07:44.159
I love you guys.

07:44.161 --> 07:45.443
We love you, too.

07:45.445 --> 07:47.629
You know, when I think about it,

07:47.631 --> 07:50.382
you guys are
my only real family.

07:50.384 --> 07:52.384
Oh, Walden, that's so...

07:52.386 --> 07:54.886
Horrible.

07:54.888 --> 07:56.171
Okay.

07:56.173 --> 07:58.590
Saved your life, but whatever.

07:58.592 --> 08:00.658
My life is pathetic.

08:00.660 --> 08:03.695
I mean, thank you guys so much
for being here.

08:03.697 --> 08:06.531
But you're not good enough!

08:06.533 --> 08:09.350
Okay, now it sounds
like my family.

08:09.352 --> 08:11.186
Um...

08:11.188 --> 08:12.188
Maybe you should rest.

08:12.189 --> 08:13.605
You know, just go
to your happy place.

08:13.607 --> 08:15.156
I know a shortcut.

08:15.158 --> 08:16.158
Say when.

08:16.159 --> 08:17.525
Whe...

08:17.527 --> 08:19.994
(squeals)

08:19.996 --> 08:23.164
Dressed as a nun,
giving some guy morphine--

08:23.166 --> 08:26.084
boy, does this take me
back to high school.

08:32.175 --> 08:34.459
Hey, how you feeling?

08:34.461 --> 08:35.543
I'm all right.

08:35.545 --> 08:37.345
Well, uh, I know

08:37.347 --> 08:39.597
something that'll
make you feel better.

08:39.599 --> 08:41.933
I made some of my famous
three bean salad.

08:42.803 --> 08:44.269
The secret--

08:44.271 --> 08:46.521
(whispers):
I use four beans.

08:48.008 --> 08:50.225
Garbanzo.

08:50.227 --> 08:51.726
Shh.

08:51.728 --> 08:54.229
You ever look out at the ocean

08:54.231 --> 08:56.498
and think about how small
and insignificant you are?

08:56.500 --> 08:59.818
I don't need the ocean;
I can just call my mother.

08:59.820 --> 09:01.402
I almost died, Alan.

09:01.404 --> 09:03.071
But the important thing is
you didn't.

09:03.073 --> 09:05.156
So, now you just have
to listen to your doctors,

09:05.158 --> 09:06.491
don't stress about anything
and relax.

09:06.493 --> 09:09.077
(shrill laughing)
(screams)

09:09.079 --> 09:11.379
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

09:13.717 --> 09:15.667
Sorry.

09:15.669 --> 09:17.836
That was supposed to scare the
life out of trick-or-treaters,

09:17.838 --> 09:19.087
not you.

09:19.089 --> 09:20.138
This sucks!

09:20.140 --> 09:22.474
How am I the one
with a stent in my heart?

09:22.476 --> 09:24.259
I'm healthy, I-I'm fit.

09:24.261 --> 09:26.094
You sit in front
of the TV every night,

09:26.096 --> 09:28.213
shoveling a pint of ice cream
down your throat.

09:28.215 --> 09:29.764
Hey, I eat my feelings,

09:29.766 --> 09:32.100
and you are sending me
right back to the freezer.

09:32.102 --> 09:33.434
You know, it just goes to show,

09:33.436 --> 09:35.270
your life can end
in the blink of an eye.

09:35.272 --> 09:37.105
One day you're here,
the next day you're gone.

09:37.107 --> 09:38.606
That's why I live
by the philosophy

09:38.608 --> 09:41.409
“One day I'm here,
the next day I'm still here.”

09:41.411 --> 09:45.613
You know, if-if I would have
died, who would have missed me?

09:45.615 --> 09:48.333
What are you talking about?
I would, Berta would.

09:48.335 --> 09:50.919
A-And you just got an e-mail
from Netflix the other day

09:50.921 --> 09:53.037
that literally said,
“We miss you.”

09:54.708 --> 09:58.459
You know, other than you guys
and my mom, I got nobody.

09:58.461 --> 10:00.128
At least you got Jake.

10:00.130 --> 10:02.297
Well, that's true.

10:02.299 --> 10:04.432
I'll always have
my little guy.

10:04.434 --> 10:06.267
Although, in his last e-mail,

10:06.269 --> 10:09.637
he, uh, asked me when the
Fourth of July was this year.

10:11.808 --> 10:14.359
But, yes, I'm very lucky.

10:14.361 --> 10:17.812
Do you know how much
I would give to have a kid

10:17.814 --> 10:20.698
who didn't understand
the concept of a calendar?

10:22.319 --> 10:24.152
All I have is money.

10:24.154 --> 10:25.537
Yeah.

10:25.539 --> 10:28.690
'Cause I wouldn't give up Jake
for a billion dollars.

10:31.378 --> 10:33.378
I got to make some changes.

10:33.380 --> 10:34.495
Changes are good.

10:34.497 --> 10:36.164
Uh, you know,
I remember when I switched

10:36.166 --> 10:38.082
from&lt;i> American Idol&lt;/i> to&lt;i> The Voice.&lt;/i>

10:39.169 --> 10:40.501
My life turned around

10:40.503 --> 10:42.887
like Blake Shelton's chair.

10:42.889 --> 10:44.672
You know what?

10:44.674 --> 10:46.724
I want to have a kid of my own.

10:46.726 --> 10:48.509
What?

10:48.511 --> 10:51.012
Yeah, I want something
to give my life meaning.

10:51.014 --> 10:53.565
I want somebody
I can love unconditionally.

10:53.567 --> 10:56.017
Someone I can teach,
someone I can nurture,

10:56.019 --> 10:57.936
someone I can leave
all this to.

10:57.938 --> 10:59.187
Well...

10:59.189 --> 11:02.690
I mean, I don't know
what to say, except...

11:02.692 --> 11:04.442
Papa?

11:04.444 --> 11:06.527
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

11:14.141 --> 11:15.702
Have you thought
this through?

11:15.703 --> 11:17.053
Having a kid
is a lot of work.

11:17.055 --> 11:20.339
Having you is
a lot of work.

11:20.341 --> 11:22.541
You know, having a child
would give my life meaning.

11:22.543 --> 11:24.210
Otherwise, all this
has been for nothing,

11:24.212 --> 11:25.628
and that's difficult
to accept.

11:25.630 --> 11:27.012
You know
what's difficult?

11:27.014 --> 11:29.598
Removing a marble
your kid shoved up his nose.

11:29.600 --> 11:30.883
I did something like that.

11:30.885 --> 11:32.218
I jammed a penny up there.

11:32.220 --> 11:35.020
I was trying to get a gumball
to fall out of my butt.

11:35.022 --> 11:36.972
But a kid
is permanent.

11:36.974 --> 11:38.274
It's not like you're dating.

11:38.276 --> 11:40.559
You can't just stop calling
or change your number

11:40.561 --> 11:42.695
or fake your own death
because they annoy you.

11:42.697 --> 11:44.146
You do that to women?

11:44.148 --> 11:45.548
No, they do it to me.

11:47.285 --> 11:49.885
Look, I-I'm sorry if it feels
like I'm being negative,

11:49.887 --> 11:52.254
because the truth is,
you know, kids are amazing.

11:52.256 --> 11:54.490
But you just had
this big health scare,

11:54.492 --> 11:56.492
and you're probably not
in the best frame of mind

11:56.494 --> 11:57.743
to make life decisions.

11:57.745 --> 12:00.713
I mean, this morning,
you cried at a beer commercial.

12:00.715 --> 12:04.316
Yeah, but the horse and
the puppy were best friends!

12:04.318 --> 12:05.785
Look,

12:05.787 --> 12:07.670
having a heart attack
didn't make me realize

12:07.672 --> 12:10.339
I want to have a kid,
it made me realize

12:10.341 --> 12:12.057
I don't want to live
another day without one.

12:12.059 --> 12:13.809
It was like a wake-up call.

12:13.811 --> 12:15.227
All right.

12:15.229 --> 12:19.398
If you really want to do this,
I will be here to support you.

12:19.400 --> 12:20.866
From my room.

12:20.868 --> 12:24.136
Which, FYI, is way too drafty
to use as a nursery.

12:24.138 --> 12:26.405
Don't worry.
You're not going anywhere.

12:26.407 --> 12:27.857
Sweet! Let's get that kid!

12:28.609 --> 12:29.942
So, uh, who's the lucky lady

12:29.944 --> 12:31.827
who's gonna receive your seed?

12:31.829 --> 12:34.163
See, you just put
your creepy little finger

12:34.165 --> 12:35.548
right on the problem.

12:36.701 --> 12:39.168
I haven't exactly been
successful in love.

12:39.170 --> 12:43.372
It's like I'm running JavaScript
and women are running HTML5.

12:44.842 --> 12:47.343
Talking like that is part
of the problem, isn't it?

12:47.345 --> 12:48.544
Yeah.

12:48.546 --> 12:50.713
And it's weird, because
your package is perfect.

12:52.650 --> 12:55.551
And... and by “package,”
I don't mean your package,

12:55.553 --> 12:59.572
I mean your...
package.

13:00.391 --> 13:03.058
Although, that is also
a showstopper.

13:03.060 --> 13:06.028
Okay, I can't believe that
this is not the first time

13:06.030 --> 13:08.898
I've said this, but stop
looking at my penis.

13:11.385 --> 13:13.452
Well, now that
you've mentioned it,

13:13.454 --> 13:16.338
I can't stop looking.

13:16.340 --> 13:18.624
It's like the elephant's trunk
in the room.

13:20.411 --> 13:22.378
Don't worry,
you'll-you'll find somebody.

13:22.380 --> 13:24.380
And, you know,
it goes without saying

13:24.382 --> 13:27.466
that if I could, I would
happily bear you a child.

13:28.436 --> 13:31.637
Okay, I wish all of this
had gone without saying.

13:31.639 --> 13:33.389
You doing okay?

13:33.391 --> 13:35.007
Yeah, I'm good.

13:35.009 --> 13:37.810
He wants to have a kid.
Now all he needs is a woman.

13:37.812 --> 13:40.062
Would you consider
a pregnant stripper?

13:40.898 --> 13:42.731
Uh, no.

13:42.733 --> 13:45.568
Well, that rules out
both my granddaughters.

13:51.776 --> 13:53.909
Morning. Did you
take your pills?

13:53.911 --> 13:55.311
Yep.

13:55.313 --> 13:57.663
Are you lying to me
or are you lying to yourself?

13:57.665 --> 13:59.048
(rattling)

14:00.167 --> 14:02.885
They're too big.
It's hard to swallow.

14:03.704 --> 14:05.371
If you say
“that's what she said,”

14:05.373 --> 14:07.039
I will kill you.

14:07.041 --> 14:08.123
You know what she said?

14:08.125 --> 14:10.543
“Take your pills.
I care about you.”

14:10.545 --> 14:11.827
Fine.

14:11.829 --> 14:14.179
Do you know how long
it takes to get a baby?

14:14.181 --> 14:17.383
Well, I know it takes, uh,
five months of mood swings

14:17.385 --> 14:20.469
and four months of not
wanting to be touched.

14:20.471 --> 14:23.522
And who knows what my ex-wife
was going through.

14:23.524 --> 14:24.723
I was just
researching surrogacy,

14:24.725 --> 14:26.792
and they say that once
you choose a great candidate,

14:26.794 --> 14:28.260
it can take
up to three years

14:28.262 --> 14:30.229
before you have
a baby in your arm.

14:30.231 --> 14:31.630
I can't wait that long.

14:31.632 --> 14:34.099
I mean, who knows if I'll even
still want a kid by then?

14:34.101 --> 14:35.534
Tell me about it.

14:35.536 --> 14:38.821
Six months into Jake's life,
I was like, “Check, please!”

14:38.823 --> 14:40.739
I was kidding.

14:40.741 --> 14:42.775
As was I.

14:45.046 --> 14:46.412
Okay.

14:46.414 --> 14:48.631
I've narrowed down my options
to either adoption

14:48.633 --> 14:50.149
or seeing if
Brad and Angelina

14:50.151 --> 14:52.234
have an extra one
they could throw me.

14:52.236 --> 14:54.253
Uh, you know, if you really
want to adopt...

14:54.255 --> 14:57.389
For the last time, Alan,
I am not adopting you!

14:57.391 --> 14:59.174
But, Papa...

14:59.176 --> 15:01.377
Ah! All right.

15:04.765 --> 15:06.815
I already reached out
to a lawyer

15:06.817 --> 15:08.601
who specializes in adoption.

15:08.603 --> 15:10.936
Well, you're a perfect
candidate to adopt.

15:10.938 --> 15:13.188
I mean, you're highly educated,
you're likeable,

15:13.190 --> 15:15.024
uh, you have a stable
home environment...

15:15.026 --> 15:19.328
Financially secure,
no criminal record, handsome.

15:19.330 --> 15:23.115
I-I don't... I don't think
handsome really comes into play.

15:23.117 --> 15:25.618
Doesn't it, Alan?

15:25.620 --> 15:27.736
No, I don't think so.

15:29.957 --> 15:31.340
Doesn't it?

15:31.342 --> 15:33.142
You're being ridiculous.

15:33.144 --> 15:34.710
Am I?

15:36.597 --> 15:39.014
I will steal you a baby.

15:40.601 --> 15:42.468
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

15:42.470 --> 15:44.803
So, as you can see,
finances are not an issue.

15:44.805 --> 15:46.472
I have a lot of
extra free time,

15:46.474 --> 15:49.775
and I know I can provide
a loving, nurturing home.

15:50.611 --> 15:52.444
You okay?

15:52.446 --> 15:55.314
Are you?

15:55.316 --> 15:57.549
Seriously, do I need
to call someone?

15:58.369 --> 15:59.618
Never mind.

15:59.620 --> 16:00.736
What's important is that

16:00.738 --> 16:02.488
I will coach the hell
out of the Braves.

16:02.490 --> 16:03.739
Excuse me?

16:03.741 --> 16:05.708
It'll be the name of
my son's tee-ball team.

16:05.710 --> 16:07.459
Pretty Pink Ponies,
if it's a girl.

16:07.461 --> 16:09.495
You know what,
if my son wants to play

16:09.497 --> 16:11.664
for the Pretty Pink Ponies,
then so be it.

16:11.666 --> 16:13.716
Tolerant.

16:14.552 --> 16:15.801
Well, Mr. Schmidt,

16:15.803 --> 16:18.087
you are obviously
more than qualified.

16:18.089 --> 16:19.021
Thank you.

16:19.023 --> 16:20.172
That said, I'd start looking

16:20.174 --> 16:21.473
at Golden Retriever puppies,

16:21.475 --> 16:22.891
'cause there's no way
you're getting a baby.

16:22.893 --> 16:24.727
Well, I don't understand.

16:24.729 --> 16:26.428
You just said that
I'm more than qualified.

16:26.430 --> 16:27.479
And you are.

16:27.481 --> 16:28.814
But you're a single guy,

16:28.816 --> 16:31.066
and the system is really geared
towards married couples.

16:31.068 --> 16:32.701
That's racist.

16:32.703 --> 16:35.304
Uh, no, it's not.

16:35.306 --> 16:36.705
Then it's sexist.

16:36.707 --> 16:38.273
Nope.

16:38.275 --> 16:40.743
Well, it's some kind of “sist.”

16:40.745 --> 16:43.028
Look, I'm not saying
it's impossible, okay?

16:43.030 --> 16:44.446
Just that it's difficult.

16:44.448 --> 16:47.249
You're in line behind families
that already have children,

16:47.251 --> 16:48.817
married couples, single women...

16:48.819 --> 16:49.835
Anyone else?

16:49.837 --> 16:51.537
What, sweat shops? Circuses?

16:51.539 --> 16:53.005
The Vienna Boys' Choir?

16:53.007 --> 16:55.174
Look, I wish
I had better news, okay?

16:55.176 --> 16:57.593
If you were married,
this would be a slam dunk.

16:57.595 --> 16:59.294
Okay, you don't get it.

16:59.296 --> 17:01.680
Marriage is not
an option for me.

17:01.682 --> 17:04.016
Okay, I understand
you're frustrated...

17:04.018 --> 17:06.135
No, what's frustrating
is that every woman I meet

17:06.137 --> 17:07.386
runs screaming from me!

17:07.388 --> 17:08.437
I was married before
and she left me

17:08.439 --> 17:10.022
and I tried to commit suicide.

17:10.024 --> 17:11.356
Don't write that down.

17:11.358 --> 17:12.775
Why are you
writing that down?!

17:12.777 --> 17:13.942
No, no...

17:13.944 --> 17:15.360
Then I proposed
to two other women,

17:15.362 --> 17:16.645
and they both shot me down.

17:16.647 --> 17:18.113
I am incapable of maintaining

17:18.115 --> 17:20.032
a long-term relationship
with anybody.

17:20.034 --> 17:21.734
Now, give me a frickin' baby!

17:21.736 --> 17:23.152
Okay.

17:23.154 --> 17:24.203
I think we're done here.

17:24.205 --> 17:25.871
No, we are
not done here!

17:25.873 --> 17:27.906
I almost died wearing
a bedazzled jumpsuit

17:27.908 --> 17:29.291
and my life
needs meaning.

17:29.293 --> 17:31.210
Stop writing
things down!

17:37.468 --> 17:38.584
Mmm.

17:38.586 --> 17:40.335
Hey, how'd it go?
What kind of world...

17:40.337 --> 17:41.220
Uh-oh.

17:41.222 --> 17:42.588
...are we living in

17:42.590 --> 17:45.507
where any two high school kids
with a broken condom

17:45.509 --> 17:47.676
can screw behind
an Applebee's Dumpster,

17:47.678 --> 17:49.511
have a baby,
give it up for adoption,

17:49.513 --> 17:53.432
but not have it go to
an adult who is upstanding,

17:53.434 --> 17:56.852
responsible,
and, might I add, handsome...

17:58.239 --> 18:00.272
...simply because
every woman I meet

18:00.274 --> 18:01.607
eventually grows to loathe me?

18:01.609 --> 18:03.442
And because of that,
the Pretty Pink Ponies

18:03.444 --> 18:05.778
will not have a tee-ball coach!

18:05.780 --> 18:07.546
So it didn't go well?

18:07.548 --> 18:09.114
(mocking):
No, it did not go well.

18:09.116 --> 18:12.201
All right, well, uh,
first things first.

18:12.203 --> 18:14.253
Uh, how about we get
you a little Zin

18:14.255 --> 18:15.571
to calm your nerves?

18:15.573 --> 18:16.955
It's just not fair.

18:16.957 --> 18:17.957
I know, I know.

18:17.958 --> 18:19.341
Uh, thank you.

18:19.343 --> 18:21.627
Just because I'm single,
I'm not a fit parent?

18:21.629 --> 18:23.212
Did they say that to you?

18:24.048 --> 18:26.799
That's how I felt.

18:26.801 --> 18:28.016
Apparently, the whole system

18:28.018 --> 18:30.052
is geared towards
married couples.

18:30.054 --> 18:31.553
And-and single guys
are not welcome.

18:31.555 --> 18:33.388
Like a Studio City
swingers party.

18:33.390 --> 18:35.691
Exactly.

18:35.693 --> 18:37.693
Wait, what?

18:37.695 --> 18:39.978
Nothing. So, uh, did you
tell her everything?

18:39.980 --> 18:42.314
I mean, how you're successful,
you're warm, you're caring...

18:42.316 --> 18:44.032
I told her everything.
Did you give her the smile?

18:44.034 --> 18:45.868
Of course I gave
her the smile.

18:45.870 --> 18:47.703
She thought I was
having a stroke.

18:48.539 --> 18:49.805
So nothing worked?

18:49.807 --> 18:52.074
No. Even if I hadn't been
escorted out by security,

18:52.076 --> 18:54.293
I still don't think
they were giving me a kid.

18:54.295 --> 18:56.411
Wow, I'm, uh...
I'm really sorry.

18:56.413 --> 18:57.830
You know, it's ridiculous.

18:57.832 --> 19:00.632
Why-why are married people
automatically better parents?

19:00.634 --> 19:03.218
My mom was married six
times; didn't help her.

19:03.220 --> 19:05.721
See, and I would've been
a great dad.

19:05.723 --> 19:07.339
I would've played
catch with him,

19:07.341 --> 19:08.473
I would've read to him,

19:08.475 --> 19:10.225
I would've waited
till he went to sleep

19:10.227 --> 19:12.344
before I smoked pot.

19:12.346 --> 19:14.980
Already got my mom beat.

19:14.982 --> 19:16.182
But-but you shouldn't give up.

19:16.183 --> 19:17.766
I mean, you might
still find somebody.

19:17.768 --> 19:19.318
No, I don't want
to marry somebody

19:19.320 --> 19:20.769
just to marry somebody.

19:20.771 --> 19:22.354
It's got to be the right person.

19:22.356 --> 19:24.156
Ooh, or Mila Kunis.

19:25.242 --> 19:26.575
I get it.

19:26.577 --> 19:27.693
That's hard to find.

19:27.695 --> 19:29.494
(timer dings)
Oh, that's my banana bread.

19:29.496 --> 19:31.146
I love your banana bread.

19:31.148 --> 19:32.080
I know.

19:32.082 --> 19:33.665
I made it hoping
we could celebrate,

19:33.667 --> 19:36.568
but it works on
a sad tummy, too.

19:37.438 --> 19:39.388
Oh, what would I do without you?

19:39.390 --> 19:42.090
I hope you never have
to find out. (chuckles)

19:43.827 --> 19:45.794
What?

19:45.796 --> 19:49.414
You are... always there for me.

19:49.416 --> 19:51.216
Yeah, and-and you're always
there for me.

19:51.218 --> 19:52.734
We're best friends.

19:54.889 --> 19:58.273
What if we were
more than friends?

19:59.143 --> 20:02.477
Like...

20:02.479 --> 20:04.696
super friends?

20:09.570 --> 20:11.019
Alan Harper,

20:11.021 --> 20:12.671
will you marry me?

20:16.610 --> 20:18.877
♪&lt;i> Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:26.300 --> 20:30.636
Are you seriously
asking me to marry you?

20:33.591 --> 20:35.858
I can't believe
this is happening.

20:38.189 --> 20:41.423
And I always thought Alan
would be the one on his knees.

20:41.425 --> 20:47.925
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>
